<h2>Requirement description</h2>

<p>
This requirement is concerned with selecting technologies that are proportionate to the business problem and capable of meeting the service's non-functional requirements.
</p>

<p>
Technology choices should be driven by user needs, business objectives and operational requirements. Teams should avoid selecting technologies that are unnecessarily complex, expensive or difficult to operate, while also avoiding solutions that are too simplistic to meet reliability, security, scalability, resilience or performance needs.
</p>

<p>
The objective is to achieve an appropriate balance between capability, complexity, cost and risk.
</p>

<p>
<strong>In simple terms:</strong><br>
Choose technology that is fit for purpose. Avoid both unnecessarily complicated solutions and solutions that are too limited for the service's needs.
</p>

